Kind: widen
Issue: #642
Holds open: thread_doswapin() just after it marks the stack in, and thread_swapout() just before it unwires it, for 100 ms each, for the activation of the -Q arm that is running -- so [2] and [3] meet their state every time, and the fixed tree must still pass with the windows open
Run: --entry 25 600 -smp 4

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/thread_swap.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/thread_swap.c
index 59416950..6653e587 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/thread_swap.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/thread_swap.c
@@ -237,6 +237,13 @@ int	maxslp = MAXSLP;
 unsigned int	thread_swapouts;
 unsigned int	thread_swapins;
 
+/*
+ * ablations/642-widen-swap.patch: the activation whose swap-in and swap-out
+ * are held open, and the spin that holds them (in -Q's test).
+ */
+thread_act_t	swap_widen_act;
+extern void	swap_widen_spin(void);
+
 #ifndef MAX_SWAP_RATE
 #define MAX_SWAP_RATE	60
 #endif
@@ -491,6 +498,8 @@ void thread_doswapin(
